{"assets":["/statement-assets/b4550febff01a647e69dab8708f6d5c24d2513b9550172e4f4f227816febcd00.png","/statement-assets/5f31f0c230402d9c486a509f3462127a0fc3ebc6f8229bdf5e323a8de93de7d4.png","/statement-assets/a462ccd647252bdd4fb7a49c1507e2da22c0c24f3109cd6680fed7a85c446683.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1278","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Segment Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As the name of the task implies, you are asked to do some work with segments and trees."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that a tree is a connected undirected graph such that there is exactly one simple path between every pair of its vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$n$$$ segments $$$[l_1, r_1], [l_2, r_2], \\dots, [l_n, r_n]$$$, $$$l_i \\lt r_i$$$ for every $$$i$$$. It is guaranteed that all segments' endpoints are integers, and all endpoints are unique — there is no pair of segments such that they start in the same point, end in the same point or one starts in the same point the other one ends."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's generate a graph with $$$n$$$ vertices from these segments. Vertices $$$v$$$ and $$$u$$$ are connected by an edge if and only if segments $$$[l_v, r_v]$$$ and $$$[l_u, r_u]$$$ intersect and neither of it lies fully inside the other one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, pairs $$$([1, 3], [2, 4])$$$ and $$$([5, 10], [3, 7])$$$ will induce the edges but pairs $$$([1, 2], [3, 4])$$$ and $$$([5, 7], [3, 10])$$$ will not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine if the resulting graph is a tree or not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of segments."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the next $$$n$$$ lines contain the description of the $$$i$$$-th segment — two integers $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le l_i \\lt r_i \\le 2n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that all segments borders are pairwise distinct. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the resulting graph is a tree and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n9 12\n2 11\n1 3\n6 10\n5 7\n4 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 3\n2 4\n5 9\n6 8\n7 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n5 8\n3 6\n2 9\n7 10\n1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The graph corresponding to the first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b4550febff01a647e69dab8708f6d5c24d2513b9550172e4f4f227816febcd00.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The graph corresponding to the second example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5f31f0c230402d9c486a509f3462127a0fc3ebc6f8229bdf5e323a8de93de7d4.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The graph corresponding to the third example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a462ccd647252bdd4fb7a49c1507e2da22c0c24f3109cd6680fed7a85c446683.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1278D","schema":2,"source